WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.410
Musa Dagh, the Mountain of Moses,

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.512
rises from the Mediterranean coast
north of the bay of Antioch.

3
00:00:09.552 --> 00:00:12.274
Below it lay six Armenian villages.

4
00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:17.624
In the summer of 1915 they received
the order for deportation,

5
00:00:17.664 --> 00:00:20.201
and they knew what deportation meant.

6
00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:22.616
Most villagers refused to go.

7
00:00:22.656 --> 00:00:24.506
More than 4,000 people

8
00:00:24.546 --> 00:00:27.663
drove their flocks up the mountain
and dug in.

9
00:00:28.023 --> 00:00:31.373
With Movses Ter-Kalustian
among their leaders,

10
00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:33.593
some 600 fighters blocked the paths

11
00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.552
and threw the attackers back
again and again.

12
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:39.242
The villagers sewed
two great banners:

13
00:00:39.282 --> 00:00:43.473
a red cross, and the words
'Christians in distress: rescue'.

14
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:48.005
On 5 September the French cruiser
Guichen saw the signals.

15
00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:50.555
From 12 September, five French ships

16
00:00:50.595 --> 00:00:53.675
carried about 4,000 Armenians
to Port Said,

17
00:00:53.715 --> 00:00:56.623
and the mountain
had never been taken.

18
00:00:56.983 --> 00:01:00.278
Hold Musa Dagh until the ships come.

